    "lawCode": "Amd §740, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2736\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to eliminating a disincentive\nfor whistleblowers\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nWhistleblowers in NY are currently barred from bringing any other legal\nclaims they may have if they choose to bring a whistleblower claim.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill eliminates a self-contradictory provision in Labor Law § 740\nwhich purports not to diminish the rights of whistleblowers but then\nsays that they cannot assert any other claims if they bring a whistle-\nblower claim, thus diminishing the rights of whistleblowers in compar-\nison to other citizens.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe statute as currently written is contrary to the ordinary rule of law\nthat a litigant should bring all claims in one action in one forum.\nThus, by requiring a litigant not to do so, and to act against normal\npractice, the existing provision is a trap for the unwary. In addition,\nit is counter-intuitive to penalize a whistleblower who may have other\ncauses of action, such as breach of an employment contract, by requiring\nthe whistleblower to give up such other causes of action in order to\nbring a whistleblower claim. Whistleblower claims are particularly\nimportant because, by exposing problems in government and society, the\nneed for reform is identified.  Discouraging legitimate whistleblower\nclaims is a barrier to remedying corruption.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nAssembly\n\n2017 - Passed Assembly\n2018 - Passed Assembly\n\nSenate:\n\n2017 - Referred to Rules\n2018 - Referred to Labor\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
